  "answer": "To reduce the risk of an agent choosing unsuitable actions because key environment parameters (like gravity) are hidden, making different environments appear identical, it is proposed to use recurrent policies (such as LSTMs) trained under dynamics randomization (https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.00336). This works through a mechanism where recurrent policy architectures capture the agent's state-action history, allowing their hidden state to summarize past observations and implicitly infer the hidden environment parameters (https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.00336). This extra information enables the agent to identify the optimal policy and choose the correct actions for each environment variant (https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.00336)."
